/* book: lead: An ideal transformer is a lossless two-coil block that changes AC voltage, current and impedance by the turns ratio alone. It assumes no winding resistance, no core loss, infinite core permeability and perfect coupling. A linear transformer is the practical coupled-coil model: finite self-inductances L₁ and L₂ and mutual inductance M. The ideal case is its limit. Transformers appear in phone charg */
