/* book Worked example: Q: An ideal transformer has N₁ = 500 turns, N₂ = 100 turns, primary voltage 230 V rms and a 10 Ω load on the secondary. Find V₂, I₂, I₁ and Zin.
   1. Turns ratio n = N₂/N₁ = 100/500 = 0.2.
   2. Secondary voltage V₂ = nV₁ = 0.2 × 230 V = 46 V rms.
   3. Secondary current I₂ = V₂/ZL = 46 V / 10 Ω = 4.6 A rms.
   4. Primary current I₁ = nI₂ = 0.2 × 4.6 A = 0.92 A rms.
   5. Input impedance Zin = (N₁/N₂)²ZL = (500/100)² × 10 Ω = 25 × 10 Ω = 250 Ω.
   6. Power check: V₁I₁ = 230 × 0.92 = 211.6 W and V₂I₂ = 46 × 4.6 = 211.6 W.
   Answer: V₂ = 46 V rms, I₂ = 4.6 A rms, I₁ = 0.92 A rms and Zin = 250 Ω. */
