/* book Worked example 2: Q: A linear transformer has L₁ = 0.2 H, L₂ = 0.8 H and M = 0.3 H. It is driven by 10∠0° V at ω = 100 rad/s and feeds a 10 Ω load. Find k, Zin, I₁, |I₂| and the load power.
   1. k = M/√(L₁L₂) = 0.3/√0.16 = 0.3/0.4 = 0.75.
   2. Reactances: ωL₁ = 20 Ω, ωL₂ = 80 Ω, ωM = 30 Ω, so (ωM)² = 900 Ω².
   3. Reflected impedance: 900/(10 + j80) = 900(10 − j80)/(10² + 80²) = (9000 − j72 000)/6500 = 1.385 − j11.077 Ω.
   4. Zin = j20 + 1.385 − j11.077 = 1.385 + j8.923 Ω = 9.03∠81.2° Ω.
   5. I₁ = 10/(9.03∠81.2°) = 1.107∠−81.2° A.
   6. |I₂| = ωM|I₁|/|10 + j80| = 30 × 1.107/80.62 = 0.412 A.
   7. Load power: 0.412² × 10 = 1.70 W. Check: |I₁|² × Re(Zin) = 1.107² × 1.385 = 1.70 W, so all the input power reaches the load.
   Answer: k = 0.75, Zin = 1.385 + j8.923 Ω, I₁ = 1.107∠−81.2° A, |I₂| = 0.412 A, load power 1.70 W. */
