/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - A coil on a core drives flux round the core.
   - The path opposes flux.
   - Φ = F/R = NI / (l/(μA))
   - Here φ is flux in Wb; F is MMF in A; R is reluctance in A/Wb; N is turns; I is current in A; l is path length in m; A is area in m²; μ is permeability in H/m.
   - Flux density B is flux per area: B = Φ/A, in tesla (T).
   - In a series magnetic circuit, the same flux passes through every part.
   - In a parallel magnetic circuit, two or more paths share the same MMF between the same two points.
   - An air gap has μr = 1, so Rgap = lg/(μ₀A).
   - Rcore = lc/(μ₀μrA), Rgap = lg/(μ₀A)
   - Here lc is core length in m; lg is gap length in m; A is area in m²; μ₀ = 4π×10⁻⁷ H/m; μr is relative permeability; R is in A/Wb.
*/
